// Generated from validated Bard song and jingle mechanics. Do not edit.
export const bardSongs=[{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:boom","name":"Boom","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"elemental (lightning/jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"one creature","duration":"instantaneous; concentration penalty lasts 1d3 rounds","save":"Fortitude partial","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"A loud thundercrack is created next to the ear of your target. He instantly suffers 1 point of non-elemental damage. In addition, he must make a Fortitude save or suffer a –2 penalty to Concentration checks for 1d3 rounds because of the ringing in the ears.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/b/boom/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:detune","name":"Detune","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"enfeebling (jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"one instrument","duration":"instantaneous; detuning persists until fixed","save":"none","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"While learning this handy jingle is not particularly encouraged at bardic colleges, it still seems to make the rounds among students. With it, you cause a single instrument within range to lose its tuning, giving Perform checks with it a –4 modifier. Re-tuning an instrument takes 1d4 rounds and usually creates a rather irate bard.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/d/detune/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:ghostharp","name":"Ghostharp","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"summoning (jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"one object","duration":"1 minute/level (dismissible)","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You prepare an object that records and replays a song previously played or sung in its vicinity. When performed, the song searches a radius of 50 feet for the lingering notes of a tune played there within the last day. It records these notes and reverberations. At your verbal command, “Play,” the ghostharp replays the music. The tune repeats until you command it to stop, or until the song’s duration comes to an end. The ghostharp does not record conversations. Its imperfect replay can’t reproduce bardic music or other magical effects, nor can it perform bard songs.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/g/ghostharp/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:ghost-sound","name":"Ghost Sound","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"illusion (jingle/figment)","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"illusory sounds","duration":"1 round/level (dismissible)","save":"Will disbelief","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"*Ghost sound* allows you to create a volume of sound that rises, recedes, approaches, or remains at a fixed place. You choose what type of sound *ghost sound* creates when performing it and cannot thereafter change the sound’s basic character.\n\nThe volume of sound created depends on your level. You can produce as much noise as four normal humes per caster level (maximum 40 humes). Thus, talking, singing, shouting, walking, marching, or running sounds can be created. The noise a *ghost sound* spell produces can be virtually any type of sound within the volume limit. A horde of rats running and squeaking is about the same volume as eight humes running and shouting. A roaring lion is equal to the noise from 16 humes, while a roaring dragon is equal to the noise from 32 humes. Anyone who hears a *ghost sound*receives a Will save to disbelieve.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/g/ghost-sound/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:giggle","name":"Giggle","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"enfeebling (jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"one creature","duration":"1 round","save":"Will negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The target suddenly finds something humorous enough to start giggling, and the laughter lasts for one full round. While the target can still move and attack normally, he is unable to speak, or use bardic abilities or cast spells that rely on verbalization, until he stops giggling.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/g/giggle/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:lullaby","name":"Lullaby","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":0,"school":"enfeebling (jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"living creatures in 10-ft.-radius burst","duration":"up to 1 + CHA modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"Any creature within the area that fails a Will save becomes drowsy and inattentive, taking a –5 penalty on Perception checks and a –2 penalty on Will saves against sleep effects while the *lullaby* is in effect.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/l/lullaby/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:rebound-sound","name":"Rebound Sound","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"non-elemental (jingle)","range":"long (400 ft. + 40 ft./level)","target":"straight line","duration":"instantaneous","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The bard plays a single tune of his instrument or holds a note with their voice, a small shockwave of sound bursting forth. This sound follows a straight path from the bard until it hits a solid surface and then rebounds back to the bard, the bard knows the exact distance between him and the object the sound hit. Rebound sound can penetrate liquids, finding the total depth of a body of water, or the bard can lower the power of the tune to stop if it would hit a liquid.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/r/rebound-sound/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:songbird","name":"Songbird","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"enhancing (jingle)","range":"personal","target":"self","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You acquire an even greater charisma when you perform. Anyone who hears or views your performance becomes favorably inclined toward you. This song grants you a +1 competence bonus on your Charisma-based checks involving any one person who saw the performance.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/songbird/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:song-of-serenity","name":"Song of Serenity","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":0,"school":"healing (jingle)","range":"30 ft.","target":"one creature per round","duration":"up to 1 + CHA modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Fortitude negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You channel positive energy through your song, rejuvenating a fatigued target. The target may ignore the effects of fatigue while targeted by this song.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/song-of-serenity/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:stage-light","name":"Stage Light","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"light (jingle)","range":"personal","target":"one following floating orb","duration":"1 minute (dismissible)","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"This song summons up a small floating orb of light that follows the bard. This light floats just above the head of the bard and flies to follow them. The stage light sheds normal light in a 30-foot radius and cannot be put out via water.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/stage-light/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:summon-instrument","name":"Summon Instrument","level":0,"kind":"jingle","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":0,"school":"summoning (jingle)","range":"0 ft.","target":"one handheld instrument","duration":"1 hour/level (dismissible)","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"This song summons one handheld musical instrument of your choice. This instrument appears in your hands or at your feet (your choice). The instrument is typical for its type. Only one instrument appears per performing, and it will play only for you. You can’t summon an instrument too large to be held in two hands. The summoned instrument disappears at the end of this song.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/summon-instrument/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:adoration","name":"Adoration","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing [ emotion , mind-affecting ]","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"target: one creature","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The target of this spell is the subject of adoration by those whom it tries to affect with Diplomacy or during performance combat. If the target is out of combat, it receives a +2 morale bonus on all Diplomacy checks it makes to influence creatures. If the creature is engaged in performance combat the target gains a +2 morale bonus on all performance combat checks.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/a/adoration/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:alter-musical-instrument","name":"Alter Musical Instrument","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"illusion (figment)","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"target: one musical instrument","duration":"1 hour/level (D)","save":"Fortitude negates (object)","spellResistance":"yes (object)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You alter an instrument so it sounds like a different kind of instrument you are familiar with. The change could be minor (such as making a lute sound like a guitar) or major (making a keyboard sound like drums). All other aspects of the instrument—such as volume, pitch, and how it is played—are unchanged. For example, a piccolo made to sound like an organ is no louder than a normal piccolo, can produce only high notes in the piccolo range, and is a wind instrument.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/a/alter-musical-instrument/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:amplify","name":"Amplify","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"area: 20-ft.-radius emanation centered on a creature, object, or point in space","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"Will negates (see text)","spellResistance":"yes (see text)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You cause an amplification of all sounds within the song’s area. This decreases the DC to hear those sounds by 20. Those creatures within the song’s area do not notice the increased amplification. Thus, anyone whose voice is amplified remains unaware of the increase in volume. The song can be centered on a creature, and the effect then radiates from the creature and moves as it moves. An unwilling creature can attempt a Will save to negate the song and can apply spell resistance, if any. Items in a creature’s possession receive the benefits of saves and spell resistance, but unattended objects and points in space do not.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/a/amplify/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:armys-paeon","name":"Army’s Paeon","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play a soft-spoken song of healing, bestowing nearby allies with HP regeneration. Each round this song is in effect, the targets gain Fast Healing 2.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/a/armys-paeon/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:clarion-call","name":"Clarion Call","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"illusion","range":"touch","target":"target: one creature","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"Fortitude negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The subject of this song gains two benefits. First, the affected creature gains the ability to create a sound like the blast of a mighty horn or trumpet simply by miming the action of sounding one. Second, the subject can speak in a booming voice that carries easily over great distances, lowering the DC of any check to hear what is said by –15.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/c/clarion-call/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:distort-speech","name":"Distort Speech","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enfeebling","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature","duration":"1 round/level","save":"Will negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You distort a creature’s vocalizations. The voice of the affected target becomes warped and incomprehensible, causing them to have 50% spell failure when casting spells with a vocal component.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/d/distort-speech/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:elemental-carol","name":"Elemental Carol","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing/elemental (any)","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play a song of the elements, bestowing your allies with a resistance to elemental spells and effects. The bard chooses an element type: dark, earth, fire, ice, light, lightning, water, or wind. Each round this song is in effect, allies within 30 feet of the bard gain a +2 morale bonus to Saving Throws against the elemental (of the chosen type) spells and effects as well as an Elemental (of the chosen type) Resistance of 5.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/e/elemental-carol/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:elemental-threnody","name":"Elemental Threnody","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enfeebling/elemental (any)","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: enemies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Fortitude negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play an elemental song, crippling your enemies by lowering their resistance to elemental spells and effects. The bard chooses an element type: dark, earth, fire, ice, light, lightning, water, or wind. Each round this song is in effect, enemies within 30 feet of the bard suffer a –2 penalty to Saving Throws against Elemental (of the chosen type) spells and effects as well as reduces elemental (of the chosen type) resistance by –5.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/e/elemental-threnody/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:fear-filled-tune","name":"Fear Filled Tune","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enfeebling [ emotion , fear , mind-affecting ]","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"target: one living creature with 5 or fewer HD","duration":"1d4 rounds or 1 round; see text","save":"Will partial","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The affected creature becomes [frightened](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#frightened).\n\nA [frightened](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#frightened) creature flees from the source of its fear as best it can. If unable to flee, it may fight. A [frightened](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#frightened) creature takes a –2 penalty on all attack rolls, saving throws, skill checks, and ability checks. A [frightened](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#frightened) creature can use special abilities, including spells, to flee; indeed, the creature must use such means if they are the only way to escape. If the subject succeeds on a Will save, it is [shaken](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#shaken) for 1 round.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/f/fear-filled-tune/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:feather-bar","name":"Feather Bar","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"target: 1 object of up to 1 cubic ft./level","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"Will negates (object)","spellResistance":"yes (object)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"Playing through a bar of beats you create a musical effect that causes an object to become lighter. The target’s weight decreases by half. If this song is cast on armor, the armor’s armor check penalty decreases by 1, though its categorization as light, medium, or heavy does not change.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/f/feather-bar/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:focusing-chant","name":"Focusing Chant","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"personal","target":"target: you","duration":"1 round/level","save":"none","spellResistance":"none","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on attack rolls, skill checks, and ability checks for the duration of the song.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/f/focusing-chant/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:foe-requiem","name":"Foe Requiem","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"non-elemental","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature/round","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play a song of destruction. Each round this song is in effect, the targeted creature suffers non-elemental damage equal to the bard’s Charisma modifier. You may only have 1 Foe Requiem/Discord song in effect.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/f/foe-requiem/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:fortuitous-beat","name":"Fortuitous Beat","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play an invigorating song, fortifying nearby allies defenses. The targets receives a +2 morale bonus to Fortitude saves.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/f/fortuitous-beat/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:hideous-laughter","name":"Hideous Laughter","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enfeebling ( compulsion ) [ mind-affecting ]","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature","duration":"1 round/level","save":"Will negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"This song afflicts the subject with uncontrollable laughter. It collapses into gales of manic laughter, falling prone. The subject can take no actions while laughing, but is not considered helpless. On the creature’s next turn, it may attempt a new saving throw to end the effect. This is a [full-round action](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/system-rules/pathfinder-basics/#full-round) that does not provoke attacks of opportunity. If this save is successful, the effect ends. If not, the creature continues laughing for the entire duration. A creature with an Intelligence score of 2 or lower is not affected. A creature whose type is different from the bard’s receives a +4 bonus on its saving throw, because humor doesn’t “translate” well.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/h/hideous-laughter/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:insidious-rhythm","name":"Insidious Rhythm","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enfeebling","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature","duration":"1 round/level","save":"Will negates","spellResistance":"yes","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"The subject takes a –4 penalty on Intelligence-based skill checks and Concentration checks due to an endlessly recycling melody stuck in its mind. Whenever the subject attempts to cast, concentrate on, or direct a spell, it must succeed on a Concentration check (DC equal to *insidious rhythm’s* save DC + spell’s level) or fail at the attempt.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/i/insidious-rhythm/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:inspirational-boost","name":"Inspirational Boost","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"see text","target":"target: allies affected by your Inspire Courage bardic performance","duration":"1 round/level","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 swift action","description":"As you finish, the song’s chant allows you to segue easily into bolstering your allies. While this song is in effect, the bonuses granted by your inspire courage bardic music increases by 1. The effect lasts until your inspire courage effect ends or this song ends, whichever comes first. If you don’t begin to use your inspire courage ability before the beginning of your next turn, the song’s effect ends.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/i/inspirational-boost/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:joyful-noise","name":"Joyful Noise","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"elemental (earth)","range":"15 ft.","target":"area: 15-ft.-radius emanation centered on you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You create sonic vibrations that negate any magical silencing effects within a 15-ft radius around you. Allies within the area of effect may ignore the effects of the [Silenced](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/status-effects/#silenced) status effect. While in the area, any silence effects continue their duration but are essentially disabled until the creature leaves the area.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/j/joyful-noise/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:knights-minne","name":"Knight’s Minne","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play the song of the knight, enhancing nearby allies Armor Class to deflect attacks better. Each round this song is in effect, the targets gain a +2 deflection bonus to Armor Class.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/k/knights-minne/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:lions-song","name":"Lion’s Song","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)","target":"targets: one creature plus one additional creature per four levels, no two of which can be more than 30 ft. apart","duration":"10 minutes; see text","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You instill courage in the subject, granting it a +4 [morale bonus](https://www.d20pfsrd.com/basics-ability-scores/glossary#TOC-Morale-Bonus) against [fear effects](https://www.d20pfsrd.com/gamemastering/other-rules/fear/) for 10 minutes. If the subject is under the influence of a fear effect when receiving the song, that effect is suppressed for the duration of the song.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/l/lions-song/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:performers-wine","name":"Performer's Wine","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"10 ft.","target":"target: 1 cu. ft./2 levels of liquid (see text)","duration":"5 minutes/level","save":"Will negates (object)","spellResistance":"yes (object)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"This song turns non-magic liquids—including spoiled, rotten, diseased, poisonous, or otherwise contaminated drinks, tears, seawater, and similar fluids—into mead or wine of average quality. This song does not prevent subsequent natural decay or spoilage.\n\nUnholy water and similar liquids of significance are spoiled by performer’s wine, but the song has no effect on creatures of any type or on magical potions or alchemical items.  \nCreatures that drink the mead or wine created by this song become sharp-witted and clear-minded, gaining a +2 enhancement bonus on all Intelligence– and Wisdom-based skill checks. This increases to a +5 bonus at caster level 9th, and to +10 (the maximum) at caster level 15th.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/p/performers-wine/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:play-instrument","name":"Play Instrument","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"personal","target":"target: you","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You may play one instrument of your choice as if you had 1 rank in the appropriate Perform skill. Instead of a conventional instrument, you may use an object as an improvised instrument, such as using a barrel as a drum or a bow as a harp, playing it as if it were crafted to make music.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/p/play-instrument/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:quick-etude","name":"Quick Etude","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play the song of fast reflexes, enhancing nearby allies Armor Class to dodge ranged attacks better. Each round this song is in effect, the targets gain a +2 dodge bonus to Armor Class against ranged attacks.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/q/quick-etude/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:reflexive-strum","name":"Reflexive Strum","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play an invigorating song, fortifying nearby allies reflexes. The targets receive a +2 morale bonus to Reflex saves.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/r/reflexive-strum/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:resonance-armor","name":"Resonance Armor","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"personal","target":"target: you","duration":"1 hour/level (D)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play a short song that forms a semi-physical barrier of sound around your body, providing a +4 armor bonus to AC. Unlike mundane armor, resonance armor entails no armor check penalty, arcane spell failure chance, or speed reduction.\n\nSince resonance armor is made of soundwaves, [sonic](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/#sonic) based attacks and effects find it harder to affect you. Any sound-based attacks like that from a [tamer’s](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/classes/core-classes/beastmaster/archetypes/tamer/) bell or another [bard’s](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/classes/core-classes/bard/) [musical power](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/classes/core-classes/bard/#musical-power) do not bypass this bonus to AC, the armor also grants you a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against [sonic](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/#sonic) effects.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/r/resonance-armor/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:saving-finale","name":"Saving Finale","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature","duration":"instantaneous","save":"with a bonus equal to the level of the song you ended – 1 (ex: ending a 2nd level song gives a saving throw bonus of +1).","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 immediate action","description":"With a flourish, you can immediately end a maintained 1st level or higher song when a creature fails a Saving Throw, allowing the subject to immediately reroll the failed Saving Throw with a bonus equal to the level of the song you ended – 1 (ex: ending a 2nd level song gives a saving throw bonus of +1).","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/saving-finale/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:sheepfoe-mambo","name":"Sheepfoe Mambo","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play a song of resistance, boosting your allies’ saving throws. Each round this song is in effect, allies within 30 feet of the bard gain a +1 morale bonus on saving throws.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/sheepfoe-mambo/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:solid-note","name":"Solid Note","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"summoning","range":"30 ft.","target":"effect: one solidified musical note","duration":"1 minute/level","save":"none","spellResistance":"no","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You give temporary physical form to a single musical note and can hang it, suspended, wherever you wish within range, allowing you to use it as hook, pulley, door blocker, or anything else your imagination desires. The exact appearance of the solid note depends on your melody. You can make it spiked or smooth, simple or convoluted, and with any color pattern you wish, however, it always has a size approximately equal to that of your outstretched hand.\n\nOnce created, the solid note resists all attempts to move it but instantly disappears if enough force or weight is brought to bear against it. The note has an effective Strength equal to 10 + your caster level. It cannot hold more weight than the equivalent of a heavy load for its Strength without disappearing. Any creature that wins an opposed Strength check against the note (by pushing open a door which the note is holding shut for example) also causes it to disappear.\n\nThe note can never deal actual harm to a creature and disappears if successfully attacked (AC 10 + your Charisma modifier) or overcome with a combat maneuver such as bull rush (CMD 2 + your base attack bonus + your Charisma modifier). Any creature obstructed by the solid note simply fails to budge it and loses that action for the round.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/solid-note/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:suit-of-the-dancer","name":"Suit of the Dancer","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"summoning","range":"personal","target":"target: you","duration":"instantaneous","save":"none","spellResistance":"yes (harmless, object)","castingTime":"1 round","description":"A strum of strings, a beat of drums, or a wave of symbols creates a wash of sound that clings onto your clothes to make them better suited to the situation.\n\nThis song allows you to replace your currently worn clothing with any stored in your Attire Space, with 1 performance you can exchange your current clothing with 1 outfit from your space. If you do not want to trade out an outfit, you can instead have the outfit appear neatly folded adjacently to the bard.\n\nStoring clothing into the bard’s Attire Space requires 1 performance of this song per outfit and it can hold a total weight of clothes equal to 10lbs per caster level.\n\nYou cannot use this song to affect any form of armor or wondrous items, unless the items are counted as clothing.\n\nAny clothes stored or changed out are cleaned as if affected by the [Magical Cleaning](https://www.finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/m/magical-cleaning/) cantrip.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/s/suit-of-the-dancer/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:toilsome-chant","name":"Toilsome Chant","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"normal","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: one creature","duration":"instantaneous","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You can perform this song as part of the action to begin an inspire competence bardic performance. The benefit of inspire competence persists for as long as is necessary to complete the target’s next skill check using the chosen skill, even if you cease your bardic performance.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/t/toilsome-chant/"},{"id":"ffd20:song:bard:willful-clash","name":"Willful Clash","level":1,"kind":"song","usageMode":"maintained","mpCost":1,"school":"enhancing","range":"30 ft.","target":"target: allies within 30 ft. of you","duration":"up to 1 + Charisma modifier rounds (maintained)","save":"Will negates (harmless)","spellResistance":"yes (harmless)","castingTime":"1 standard action","description":"You play an invigorating song, fortifying nearby allies will power. The targets receive a +2 morale bonus to Will saves.","url":"https://finalfantasyd20.com/magic/spells/w/willful-clash/"}];
